# M / B010 — code-review, configuration, custom-settings.

C R169 OL WF-010 | MUST | The review is independent and read-only (no edits or rewrites of working code unless asked); code-review is the canonical procedure that the code-reviewer agent runs and other workflows reference instead of redefining review criteria. | code review | Explicit request to change code.
C R170 OL WF-011 | MUST | Review prioritizes correctness, security/authorization, data integrity/persistence, architectural boundaries, concurrency/integration, missing meaningful tests, maintainability, then credible evidence-backed performance; style preferences are not elevated above behavioral defects; code is not reported as a violation merely for differing from an unadopted pattern. | code review | none stated
C R171 OL WF-011 | MUST | Before judging, the review reads the changed code with enough surrounding code (callers, contracts, dependencies), identifies intended behavior and tests, and reads the rules whose paths match the changed files; no review of isolated lines. | code review | none stated
C R172 OL GOV-003 | MUST NOT | Do not weaken required specified behavior or introduce unapproved product behavior: new length or numeric limits, reserved names or values, newly required fields, extra workflow restrictions, additional user-visible validation or new observable string-comparison semantics (including through database configuration or framework defaults when the specification is silent). | product behavior | Detail explicitly approved by the user with durable sources synchronized.
C R173 OL GOV-005 | DEFAULT | Internal implementation details that do not change observable product behavior are not product-behavior decisions and need no approval. | product behavior | none stated
C R174 OL WF-012 | MUST NOT | Do not manufacture review findings: no hypothetical failures without a plausible execution path, no findings to populate categories, tool output is evidence rather than authority; when no meaningful findings exist say so and state important areas that could not be verified; no filler praise. | code review | none stated
C R175 OL WF-007 | MUST | Scope deep checks by risk: the full security-scan procedure runs only when the user requested a security audit, the change is materially security-sensitive or a concrete finding justifies broader investigation; normal security review of changed code is part of every review. | code review and verification | none stated
C R176 OL TST-009 | DEFAULT | For a bug fix with plausible recurrence expect a regression test unless equivalent coverage already exists; do not request duplicate tests. | tests for bug fixes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C R177 OL GOV-021 | MUST | When an approved CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md value is added, changed or removed, record it under a stable name with value and purpose and identify and update every affected implementation, validation, configuration, test, documentation and mirrored frontend/backend surface (old value and setting name, validators and DTO constraints, Domain/Application checks, database mapping, frontend validation and UI hints, tests and test data, documentation, mirrored configuration), updating only affected behavior; search for stale references, build, test and run verify; one changed literal does not establish synchronization. | CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md changes | none stated
C R178 OL PST-009 | MUST | When a settings change affects schema constraints, indexes, column lengths or other persistence metadata: update the EF Core mapping, create the appropriate migration per the project's workflow without casually altering existing migrations, verify Development seeding remains valid and update provider-sensitive tests when provider behavior matters. | schema-affecting settings | Editing an uncommitted migration per the normal workflow.
C R180 OL GOV-001 | MUST | When SPECIFICATION.md is non-empty treat it as the authoritative source for project-specific functional requirements and observable product behavior; an empty template specification is intentional. | product requirements | Empty template specification.
C R181 OL GOV-009 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | SPECIFICATION.md and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md must not contradict each other; if they appear to conflict, stop and ask which source must be corrected rather than choosing one; resolve conflicts before changing implementation. | product sources | none stated
C R182 OL GOV-011 | MUST NOT | Never store secrets, environment-specific connection details, package versions, HTTP status codes, ports, migration identifiers or incidental implementation constants in CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md; framework defaults the project has not intentionally overridden are not settings. | CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md | none stated
C R183 OL GOV-008 | MUST | Record approved project-level tunable product limits and defaults (maximum lengths, page-size defaults and maximums, retention periods, numeric thresholds) in CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md; SPECIFICATION.md owns behavioral intent and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md the approved concrete values. | product settings | none stated
C X16 EX WF-011,WF-012 | MUST | Code-review findings are reported ordered by severity, each with severity, file/location, what is wrong, why it matters and the smallest reasonable fix, using the fixed severity scale Critical / High / Medium / Low with defined meanings. | code review output | none stated | WF-011/WF-012 govern priorities and honesty of findings; the oracle does not prescribe a findings format or severity scale. | A review that lists issues without location, impact or severity does not follow the workflow.

